    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Conversation benchmark: admission and persistence",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 89,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Match the dashboard time range to one measured concurrency step; exclude warm-up and other traffic. Client first text, final and clean EOF remain separate JSONL observations. LLM first chunk is not client TTFT. Do not subtract percentiles.\n\nAdmission timers cover selected stages, not all pre-model work. Swift alone emits runtime_binding_internal from its Python Control Plane; Weaver Rust Control Plane is not covered. Persistence timers are aggregate timing hints: store/op are not Prometheus labels, history can acquire a connection inside the SQL timer, and checkpoint pool timing can include SQL fencing. Neither timer covers all SQL or SQLx. Missing series mean unavailable evidence, not zero latency. CPU is process usage, not CPU throttling."
      }
